## 1. Deliverable and goal alignment
<What the requested work was, what the return delivers, alignment and uncertainty.>

## 2. Verified facts, claims and limits
<Evidence actually read; verified facts distinct from reported claims/inference.
No invented execution, coldboot, authority or tool-enforcement claims.>

## 3. Findings and unresolved decisions
<For each finding: ID, kind, evidence/section, observation, consequence, prior
finding link/pass, question or proposed correction.>
Functional completion: <supported / contradicted / cannot verify; why>
Reproducibility from seated instructions: <supported / contradicted / not yet
applicable because draft / cannot verify; declared prerequisites and gaps>
Preservation through change: <source-section accounting and semantic issues>
Two-pass escalation: <finding lineage/count, recorded Director reply or pending>

## 4. Learning worth preserving
<Page-local why and links; no second independent policy repository.>

## 5. One recommended next bounded action
<Advisory recommendation, not an execution release.>

## 6. Responses and disposition history — Prime/Director-owned fields
<Finding ID | fix next batch/#NN OR answer/reason OR Director escalation |
evidence/decision reference | resolution | actor/date>
<Observer writes no approval/closure. Preserve original finding and every reply.>
